<!--
  FIXTURE V-013 — vulnerable half.

  Lens:     salesforce-platform
  Topic:    permission-set-and-profile-grants
  Severity: High
  CWE:      CWE-732 (incorrect permission assignment for a critical resource)

  ONE defect: <viewAllFields>true</viewAllFields> on an object, which grants read
  on EVERY field of that object and therefore bypasses field-level security.

  This is the shape the lens's severity row used to grade Low. The row required a
  <sharingModel> of Private, Read or ControlledByParent and downgraded to Low on
  ReadWrite, reasoning that "every user already has it and the grant adds
  nothing". That reasoning is about SHARING. Care_Episode__c below is declared
  ReadWrite, so every user does already have every record — and no OWD at any
  value hands a user a field their profile cannot read. viewAllFields does. The
  downgrade therefore priced an FLS bypass at zero.

  Note what is deliberately ABSENT: this permission set contains no
  <fieldPermissions> entry for Clinical_Note__c. Under FLS its holders could not
  read that field. viewAllFields is the only reason they can, which is why an
  audit that establishes field readability from <fieldPermissions> alone reads
  this file as granting nothing.

  DO NOT EDIT to add a <fieldPermissions> block for Clinical_Note__c. The absence
  is the fixture: adding one would make the field readable by an ordinary grant
  and destroy the discriminator against Care_Episode_Reporting in this directory.

  Nothing here is deployable: no package.xml, no sfdx-project.json, no license
  assignment, no real org, no real patient data. Every label and API name was
  written for this corpus.
-->
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <label>Care Coordination Team</label>
    <description>Broadly assigned to every coordinator, scheduler and intake clerk.</description>
    <hasActivationRequired>false</hasActivationRequired>
    <objectPermissions>
        <allowCreate>true</allowCreate>
        <allowDelete>true</allowDelete>
        <allowEdit>true</allowEdit>
        <allowRead>true</allowRead>
        <modifyAllRecords>true</modifyAllRecords>
        <object>Care_Episode__c</object>
        <viewAllFields>true</viewAllFields>
        <viewAllRecords>true</viewAllRecords>
    </objectPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>true</editable>
        <field>Care_Episode__c.Episode_Status__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <tabSettings>
        <tab>Care_Episode__c</tab>
        <visibility>Visible</visibility>
    </tabSettings>
</PermissionSet>
